{"p4": {"friction": "\"This follows immediately from Corollary 0.2 applied to C=Sch', E1=P, E2=J\" passes both the depends-on test (invoked as a proof step) and the generalises boundary (instance of a general result); the extractor emitted it both ways (claims 4/8 and 14).", "doubt": "Whether a bare result locator (\"Corollary 0.3\") covers that result's proof; whether \"constructed in [6]\" counts as defines; whether applying a general theory to a specific construction (claim 1) counts as generalises.", "missing_context": "Example 4.30 and the body of Theorem 5.4 / Sections 4-5 were not in the input, so claim 7's locator part \"Example 4.30\" could only be checked against the Introduction's pointer.", "proposed_change": "Add to the depends-on/generalises boundary: when a proof consists solely of 'follows from X applied to <parameter values>', grade generalises(X, head) as the primary relation and depends-on as wrong-relation.", "process_observation": "The claim list has near-duplicates (2/6, 4/8, 13/18), and claim 10 uses the rejected relation \"cited\", which the validator should have caught before grading."}}
